         <listPerson>
            <person xml:id="HAT02" sex="1">
               <persName>
                  <roleName/>
                  <forename>Charles</forename>
                  <surname>Hatchett</surname>
                  <addName/>
               </persName>
               <birth when="1765-01-02">
                  <placeName>Long Acre, London</placeName>
               </birth>
               <death when="1847-02-10">
                  <placeName>Bellevue House</placeName>
               </death>
               <occupation>Chemist</occupation>
               <note type="editorial">
                  <p>This is likely to have been Charles Hatchett (1765-1847), a chemist and mineralogist. Hatchett married Elizabeth, the daughter of John Collick who was a Westminster magistrate. Godwin met Collick at Shield’s, 27/11/1794.</p>
                  <p>Another possibility is that it was Horatio McGeorge, an eccentric actor known as Hatchet after one of his roles.</p>
               </note>
               <bibl type="other">
                  <title>Ed Pope History Entry 27/07/2012</title>
               </bibl>
            </person>
         </listPerson>
